1) Install packages
     # dnf install nfs-utils autofs -y
2) Start and enable autofs service
     # systemctl enable autofs --now
     # systemctl status autofs
3) Test if nfs share is visible on client or not
     # showmount -e <nfs-server-ip>
4) Create same user on client and make sure do not create user’s home directory
     # useradd -u 4001 -b /rhome -M user1
     # ls /rhome  (it should be empty)
5) get the path of user home directory from /etc/passwd
     # grep user1 /etc/passwd
6) edit autofs config files
     # vi /etc/auto.master
       /-   /etc/auto.misc
     # vi /etc/auto.misc
       /rhome/user1  -fstype=nfs,rw <server_ip_address>:/remoteusers/user1
7) restart autofs service
     # systemctl restart autofs

Validation Steps:
1) ls /rhome    (it should show user1)
1) su - user1     (You should be able to switch to user1)
10) df -h     (you should see the mounted user directory)
